  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe aim to improve the upper bound for C\u2085 by leveraging structured initialization and hybrid optimization techniques. The prior approach relied on random perturbations and local optimization, which risks premature convergence. This strategy combines global exploration via periodic patterns, gradient-based refinement, and careful constraint enforcement to navigate the non-convex optimization landscape. The key bottleneck lies in escaping local optima, which the hybrid approach addresses by balancing exploration (via structured patterns) and exploitation (via local optimization with constraint handling).\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Representation: Use a piecewise constant function h: [0,2] \u2192 [0,1] sampled at n_points \u2208 \u2115 points, with h[i] \u2208 [0,1] and \u2211h[i] = n_points/2.\n- Objective: Minimize C\u2085 = max\u2096 \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)(1 - h(x + k)) dx, equivalently max_{l \u2208 [ -n_points+1, n_points-1 ]} ( (np.correlate(h, 1 - h, mode='full') * dx)[l] )\n- Constraints: \n  1. 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n  2. \u2211h[i] = n_points/2 exactly\n- Objective equivalence: The full correlation computes the integral over all lags k \u2208 [-n_points+1, n_points-1], with dx = 2/n_points.\n- Convexity: The problem is non-convex due to the product term h(x)(1 - h(x + k)), necessitating a local optimization approach with global initialization.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nInitialize with structured patterns (periodic or symmetric) and refine via SLSQP:\n    a. Parent validation: Check initial_h_values meets constraints via scaling and clipping.\n    b. Generate 5 structured initial guesses:\n        - 1. Uniform grid with alternating values\n        - 2. Sine wave sampled at n_points\n        - 3. Symmetric triangular wave\n        - 4. Gaussian-like bump function\n        - 5. Random perturbation from parent\n    c. For each candidate:\n        i. Enforce \u2211h[i] = n_points/2 via rescaling\n        ii. Formulate objective: max_correlation * dx\n        iii. Use SLSQP with bounds [0,1] and constraint \u2211h[i] = n_points/2\n    d. Maintain a global best solution, updating when a better C\u2085 is found\n    e. Perform 100 iterations of:\n        - Random perturbation (\u00b110% amplitude, \u00b15% frequency)\n        - SLSQP refinement with adaptive tolerance\n        - Objective re-evaluation\n    f. Terminate when time exceeds budget or no improvement for 50 iterations\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nDefault configuration:\n    - n_points = 500 (balance resolution and speed)\n    - Initial guess: 10% deviation from parent\n    - Perturbation amplitude: 0.05\n    - SLSQP tolerance: 1e-6\n    - Max iterations: 100\n    - Validation: re-evaluate all lags after refinement\nKey variations:\n    - Increase n_points to 600 for finer resolution\n    - Use simulated annealing for global exploration\n    - Test different wave patterns (square, triangular, exponential)\n    - Adjust perturbation amplitude based on gradient magnitude\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nTime allocation:\n    - 30% for initial structured guesses (500 steps)\n    - 50% for optimization iterations (500 steps)\n    - 20% for final refinement and validation\nRobustness measures:\n    - Track best solution in memory\n    - Time-out solver after 20s per iteration\n    - Revert to parent solution if divergence occurs\n    - Fallback: Use parent solution if no improvement after 50 iterations\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nPost-optimization checks:\n    - Ensure all h[i] \u2208 [0,1] via clipping\n    - Verify \u2211h[i] = n_points/2 within 1e-6\n    - Recompute C\u2085 via full correlation\n    - Compare with parent solution if fallback is needed\nOutput guarantees:\n    - Returns (h_values, c5_bound, n_points)\n    - h_values: 1D numpy array of floats\n    - c5_bound: float with C\u2085 value\n    - n_points: int indicating sample count\nSanity checks:\n    - Values must be in [0,1]\n    - Sum must equal n_points/2\n    - C\u2085 must be finite and calculated correctly\n    - Objectively match the evaluator's computation",
